-- HDGR_DecorQuestIndex -- the quest chains that lead to decor-rewarding quests. GENERATED by
-- housingdecorguide-tools/decorquests/build_decor_quest_index.py from build 12.1.5.70575 (wago DB2 QuestLine,
-- QuestLineXQuest, UiMap; Blizzard's quest API; the HDGProbe /decorquests runs on both factions) and that
-- folder's campaigns.json + fills.json. DO NOT HAND-EDIT.
--
-- lines[lineID] = { name, steps }  name: enUS (DB2). steps: space-separated, in quest order.
--   step = questID [ "@" spot [ "~" spot ] ] [ "#" giver ] [ "<" ender ] [ ">" questID ] [ "&" group ] [ ":" gate ]
--   spot = uiMapID [ "/" x "/" y ]   x, y = where the quest starts on that map, map percent x 10 (0-1000)
--          A second spot ("~") is the Horde one: an open quest whose giver stands in each faction's own city.
--   giver = who starts the quest (Wowhead's Start): npcID, or "o" objectID / "i" itemID (named in names);
--           absent when nobody known does. Two, "<Alliance's>/<Horde's>", on an open quest whose giver differs
--           by faction.
--   ender = who takes the quest back (Wowhead's End): npcID, or "o" objectID (named in names); absent when the
--           quest completes in the field. No spot: for a finished quest Blizzard's quest arrow points at the turn-in.
--           Two, "<Alliance's>/<Horde's>", on an open quest whose hand-in differs by faction.
--   ">" questID = the step is a breadcrumb to that quest: it drops out once the character is on that quest or did it.
--           A Series lead-in (fills.json leadIns) ships the same way.
--   "&" group = the step's any-order group on its line (1, 2, ...): quests the game hands out together, done in any
--           order. The steps of a group sit together on the line for each faction.
--   gate = [ "A" | "H" ] [ "r" raceID { "." raceID } ] [ "c" classID { "." classID } ]  |  "X"
--          A/H = that faction only; r = only these races (UnitRace's raceID); c = only these classes
--          (UnitClass's classID). No gate = anyone. X = no longer in the game (fills.json removed): nobody.
-- chains[decor questID] = lineID, or { A = lineID, H = lineID } where the factions' chains differ.
-- solo = the decor quests in no line, as steps (same grammar).
-- repeats[decor questID] = "daily" | "repeatable" | "missive": a decor quest the game lets you do again (Blizzard's
--   quest API is_daily / is_repeatable; it has no weekly flag), or a Garrison missive quest (fills.json repeats: a
--   Scouting Missive bought at the garrison starts it again). Each turn-in gives another copy of the decor.
-- starts[questID] = "map" | "own": how a step nobody gives starts: picked on a city's Scouting Map, or offered on
--   its own. ends[questID] = "tracker": a step nobody takes back is completed from the quest tracker's popup.
--   follows[questID] = "start" | "end" | "both": the NPC who gives it, takes it back, or both walks with you (an
--   escort or a companion), so it has no fixed spot. Only where Wowhead's comments say so (fills.json starts / ends /
--   follows).
-- names[o<objectID> | i<itemID>] = the name (enUS) of an object or item a step starts or ends at: the game can't
--   name an object.
-- npcNames[npcID] = the name (enUS, Wowhead's) of every NPC a step starts at, for the search box. On screen the game's
--   own name shows (NPCNameResolver), in the client's language.
-- titles = every shipped quest's name (enUS: Blizzard's quest API, else Quest Unstuck's), one "<questID>\t<name>"
--   a line, read by StaticData DecorQuests:Title; shown only while the game has no name for the quest.
-- campaigns = { { id, name, order, chapters = { { A = { lineID, name, giverNpcID }, H = ... }, ... } } }
--   order "random": the game offers the chapters one at a time, in an order it picks.
--   giverNpcID: who offers the chapter's first quest; absent when an object does (The Ring of Blood).
